{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the tablets were the work of Elohim</b>: It would have been fitting for Scripture to mention all the making of the tablets in the verse \"And He gave to Moses\" (Exodus 31:18), just as it says, \"written with the finger of Elohim.\" But it mentions it here to tell of their greatness, to say that Moses was not restrained by all this from breaking them, for his anger burned upon seeing that evil deed, and he could not hold himself back. Or according to the matter that our Rabbis mentioned (Exodus Rabbah 9:11), that the writing flew away now when it came within the boundary of the calf, in the place of impurity and sin."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:20:13.594097249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}